\title{Read AOFM Data Hub workbooks in R}
\description{
readAOFM provides a reproducible, table-oriented interface to workbooks
published by the Australian Office of Financial Management (AOFM). Users can
discover supported tables with \code{\link[=search_aofm]{search_aofm()}}, retrieve and parse one or
more tables with \code{\link[=read_aofm]{read_aofm()}}, use a family-specific reader when needed, or
save raw workbooks with \code{\link[=download_aofm_xlsx]{download_aofm_xlsx()}}. Parsed results are returned
in long-form data frames or named lists of data frames, depending on the
workbook family.
}
\details{
Public AOFM workbooks are available without package credentials. Reads and
raw downloads use HTTPS; readers stage workbooks in temporary files and
retrieve the current source on each call. Parsed CSV output is an explicit
opt-in side effect under \verb{output/}; raw workbook downloads are an explicit
operation under \verb{data/} in the current working directory. AOFM controls the
upstream URLs and workbook layouts, so source changes can require a package
update.
}
